<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  A bottlenose dolphin in side view, nose to the right.

  Filled rather than the single-weight outline ic_fish uses: this mark is drawn
  as small as 20dp in a sighting row, and an outline closes up into a smudge at
  that size. app:tint paints it in one colour either way.

  Three things carry "dolphin" rather than "fish", and each is drawn as large as
  the shape allows: a rostrum that tapers to a point off a rounded melon, a
  dorsal fin raked backwards rather than spiked upright, and horizontal notched
  flukes. A fish tail is vertical, so the flukes are the detail that has to
  survive being shrunk - which is why they are the widest thing here.
-->
